cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite this release, the source
  study, and the dataset below.
title: >-
  Code release: reproduction / attribution study of physics-based input
  features for wind-speed forecasting error (Perdigão tower tse13, v1.1)
authors:
  - name: "Perdigão attribution study v1.1 authors (anonymized for public release)"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Frozen-protocol reproduction and attribution study re-running the claim of
  Vassallo et al. (2021) that physics-based input features improve hourly wind
  speed forecast error. The calibration gate failed in all 9 conditions
  (max detection 0.73 < 0.80), so the primary statistics were not executed and
  the confirm window stayed sealed (withheld). This release contains the
  study code, calibration outputs, and final report; observation data are not
  redistributed.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Utilizing physics-based input features within a machine learning model
      to predict wind speed forecasting error
    authors:
      - family-names: Vassallo
        given-names: D.
      - family-names: Krishnamurthy
        given-names: R.
      - family-names: Fernando
        given-names: H. J. S.
    journal: "Wind Energy Science"
    volume: 6
    pages: "295-309"
    year: 2021
    doi: "10.5194/wes-6-295-2021"
  - type: dataset
    title: "Perdigão: Peña Corchado field campaign (NCAR EOL dataset 536.011, Version 1.2)"
    doi: "10.26023/ZDMJ-D1TY-FG14"
    note: "Obtain from NCAR EOL; see code/data/README.md. Last tower used: tse13."
